From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] ui-egui: translate the literals the helpers did not (print, export, info, status bar, preferences, ribbon buttons)

Phase 4 i18n pass (exploratory test, uz-Latn and ru): about 400 widget calls drew an English literal (ui.label, button, checkbox, selectable_label, hint_text, on_hover_text, selected_text, RichText::new, Slider text, links) although the catalog had the row, because only the ribbon, menu, dialog and backstage helpers went through i18n::t. Each call site now wraps its literal in crate::i18n::t; the ribbon's big and small button helpers translate their label; the print combo boxes translate the label of the chosen entry; 'Slide {} of {}', '{} of {}' and 'Version {}' are whole templates (status::slide_of) instead of format!; the Present button is t("Present") inside its padding; the status line message and the proofing language names are translated. Strings the literal scan cannot see (starter names, paper names, 'Slides:') are rows in xtask OWN_DECK_0146.
